# License

Except where a specific file, directory, or release states otherwise, this
repository contains **multiple licensing classes**, not one blanket license.
ThisIsJohnnyt licenses only the copyright and similar rights actually owned
or licensable by ThisIsJohnnyt in each class below. Third-party components
retain their own original terms regardless of anything stated here.

See [PDR-006](docs/decisions/PDR-006.md), [PDR-007](docs/decisions/PDR-007.md)
(superseded in part — see PDR-008), and
[PDR-008](docs/decisions/PDR-008.md) for the full decision history.

## 1. Gold dataset (`datasets/gold/`)

**CC BY-NC-SA 4.0** (Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike) — see
[`datasets/gold/LICENSE.md`](datasets/gold/LICENSE.md). Includes an
irrevocable historical exception: `gold_v1.0` through `gold_v1.2.3` were
published under CC-BY-4.0 before this policy existed, and that grant cannot
be revoked. See [PDR-006](docs/decisions/PDR-006.md).

## 2. Documentation (this repository's own prose: `docs/`, `README.md`,
   dataset cards, decision records, etc.)

**CC BY-NC-SA 4.0**, same terms as the dataset (Attribution, NonCommercial,
ShareAlike). Full legal text:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode.en

## 3. Software (training/inference code, e.g. `training/*.py`)

**PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0** — see
[`LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md`](LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md)
for the full text. Chosen over CC BY-NC-SA specifically for code: it's a
real software license (copyright grant, distribution/modification terms,
and an actual patent grant that CC licenses don't provide), at the cost of
not legally forcing a fork's own new modifications to stay noncommercial —
CC's ShareAlike doesn't include a source-code-delivery requirement either,
so it wouldn't have reliably delivered that guarantee anyway. See
[PDR-008](docs/decisions/PDR-008.md) for the full reasoning and the
tradeoff as presented to the product owner.

PolyForm Noncommercial's attribution mechanism is a licensor-provided
`Required Notice:` line, which every recipient must receive along with the
terms (see the license text's "Notices" section). This project's Required
Notice:

> Required Notice: Intent Recovery Model software was created by
> ThisIsJohnnyt — https://github.com/ThisIsJohnnyt/intent-recovery-model

## 4. Released model weights (`intent-recovery-model-*` releases)

**Not covered by an asserted copyright license.** Whether trained model
weights are copyrightable, and whether this project cleanly holds rights to
license them, is not legally settled. See
[`MODEL_RELEASE_NOTICE.md`](MODEL_RELEASE_NOTICE.md) for the full
explanation, the project's request (acknowledgment + noncommercial use —
a request, not an enforced condition), and third-party disclosure. See
[`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for exactly what upstream
components (`google/flan-t5-base`, Apache 2.0) each release contains and
their own terms, which are unaffected by anything in this repository.

## 5. Private data (excluded from version control)

`datasets/real_validation.jsonl` and `datasets/real_holdout.jsonl` are not
licensed at all — excluded from version control, contain the project
owner's real personal notes, never published. See
[PDR-004](docs/decisions/PDR-004.md).

## Why not "open source"

A NonCommercial restriction is incompatible with the Open Source
Initiative's Open Source Definition (criterion 6: no discrimination against
fields of endeavor). This project is precisely described as
**source-available/noncommercial**, not OSI "open source" — even though
"open source" is how the product owner describes it in plain language
elsewhere.

## GitHub license detection

GitHub's automatic license detector does not reliably recognize
CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (confirmed: not in GitHub's own license-picker table, and a
known open issue in its detection tool, `licensee/licensee#343`). PolyForm
Noncommercial 1.0.0 is a real SPDX-listed license (added in SPDX License
List v3.9), but whether GitHub's specific detector recognizes it wasn't
confirmed either way — don't assume a badge will or won't appear. Either
way, this doesn't affect legal validity — each linked file's actual text is
what governs, regardless of what the repository sidebar shows.
